threads.body:
@copilot Please make `otel.instrumentation.couchbase.emit-experimental-telemetry` the single umbrella setting for Couchbase experimental telemetry, defaulting to `false`. It should enable experimental span attributes for both Couchbase 2.x and 3.x, and also enable the SDK detail spans for Couchbase 3.x. This matches the existing HTTP convention, where `emit-experimental-telemetry` includes experimental attributes as well as other telemetry.

The next release is 3.0, so breaking changes are allowed. Remove `otel.instrumentation.couchbase.experimental-span-attributes` and its declarative equivalent, `java.couchbase.experimental_span_attributes/development`, across Couchbase 2.x and 3.x. Remove the deprecated-property fallback and warnings rather than retaining compatibility support. Keep `java.couchbase.emit_experimental_telemetry/development` as the corresponding declarative setting.

Use one effective primitive boolean, with no separate attributes flag, nullable override, or `EXPERIMENTAL_TELEMETRY_CONFIGURED` presence check. Update the tests and test variants to cover disabled and enabled umbrella behavior, and update the README, configuration metadata/generated docs, changelog migration note, and PR description accordingly. Preserve the PR's span-kind and instrumentation-scope corrections.

